Each of these buffers are stored above the area where the static arrays will be.
This results in three cases which are vulnerable:

1. If a static array with size of 3 overflows, it will overflow over the area where there are static variables.
2. If a static array with size of 3 overflows, it will overflow over another overflowed static array.
3. If a static array with size 4 overflows, it will overflow over another overflowed static array  and then the area where there are static variables.

Thus, it is vulnerable in all three cases.

