# There are multiple function calls that have the same name and arguments

This message indicates that a function declaration is used, but the code contains multiple calls of the function. The parameters in the calls must be the same. If parameters are named differently, then this warning can't be ignored. To avoid the warning, either remove the one or more unnecessary calls, or ensure that the calls have the same parameters.

## Example1

```C
// C2758_func_def.c
// compile by using: cl /WX C2758_func_def.c
// C2758 is enabled by default starting in Visual Studio 2005
void __cdecl x(int a, char b) {
  ;
}

int main() {
  x(a); // C2758
  x(a, b);
  return 0;
}
```
